Projects/UOContent/Engines/Harvest/Core/HarvestDefinition.cs

Adds one event to HarvestDefinition and raises it at the top of SendMessageTo. Nothing else changes: the
message is still sent exactly as before, and nothing in the engine subscribes.

    public static event Action<Mobile, HarvestDefinition, TextDefinition> Said;

    [MethodImpl(MethodImplOptions.AggressiveInlining)]
    public void SendMessageTo(Mobile from, TextDefinition message)
    {
+       if (Said != null && from != null)
+       {
+           try { Said(from, this, message); } catch { }
+       }
+
        if (message?.Number > 0) { from.SendLocalizedMessage(message.Number); }
        else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(message)) { from.SendMessage(message); }
    }

WHY. The harvest system already knows exactly why a swing produced nothing and says so: "There is no metal
here to mine", "Someone has gotten to the metal before you", "You loosen some rocks but fail to find any
useable ore", "You have moved too far away to continue", "Your backpack is full", "You have worn out your
tool". A player reads those. A bot has no NetState, and Mobile.SendLocalizedMessage is not virtual and writes
straight to one, so every sentence was dropped before anything could hear it.

Without the seam, a bot has to infer an empty vein from a run of quiet swings. Measured 09.09.2026, the first
time the two cases were counted apart: 16 rocks given up with the engine's bank empty against 35 that still
held ore. Two write-offs in three were wrong, and each rested the seam behind it, so the ore map shrank all
afternoon while the log reported an island running out of ore.

Patrick's order the same day: a vein counts as worked out when the bot SEES the message that there is nothing
in it. This is the seam that lets it. See Projects/BotAIv2/BotHarvest/BotHeard.cs for the listener.

DELIBERATELY NARROW. The event reports what was said and to whom; it cannot alter the message, cannot stop
the send, and a listener that throws is contained so it cannot take the harvest with it.
